        "original_id": "0f0b4db6-03b6-541c-ace4-55457342064d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fort Hunter, Schenectady, Albany County, Rotterdam\n- Roads: New York Route 146, Interstate 890, Interstate 90, New York State Route 7, Watt Street\n- Products: Crosstown Plaza\n\nFacts:\n- Fort Hunter lies along New York Route 146 near the Albany–Schenectady county line.\n- Interstate 890 is a 9.45-mile auxiliary Interstate Highway in the vicinity of Schenectady, New York.\n- Interstate 890 runs southeast–northwest from an interchange with the New York State Thruway (Interstate 90) northwest of Schenectady to another junction with the Thruway south of the city, and it passes through Downtown Schenectady.\n- Crosstown Plaza is a large strip mall in Schenectady at the Rotterdam–Schenectady line along Watt Street and New York State Route 7 near an Interstate 890 entrance.",
